# clang -S text and msil-ld --lto-emit-asm text without references of managed calls that pass a C integer for a 'valuetype' parameter that is not an enum of the integer's width: a 64-bit integer for the struct System.TimeSpan (DateTime::Add, CIL parameter 1, C parameter 2 after the 'this' handle), for the int32 enum System.DateTimeKind (DateTime::SpecifyKind, parameter 2), and for FileStream's FileMode in a stub whose msil_catch entries list System.InvalidProgramException, and an int for 'valuetype System.Int32' (Math::Abs): each stub throws InvalidProgramException with T-M7's parameter text before the member is called, outside its .try, on every runtime.
# Plan 5.20.6 MW2 as amended for MC-1 (whole-program text checks the
# declaration when it runs) and 5.20.3's T-M7 (its parameter form):
# standalone text (clang -S, llc) and msil-ld's --lto-emit-asm text bind
# nothing, so no link compares an 'enum' conversion with E's TypeDef (5.20.7
# MK2 refuses these declarations in an object link and in an --lto-emit-asm
# link with references); instead, at the very start of its body, the stub
# tests each 'enum' parameter's E: E must be an enum (typeof(E).IsEnum:
# ldtoken E, Type::GetTypeFromHandle and Type::get_IsEnum, with no local)
# and sizeof E must be the C integer's size, or the stub throws
# System.InvalidProgramException with msil-ld's text, "managed call '<f>':
# parameter <i> passes <n> bits for '<E>', which is not an enum of that
# width", <i> being the member's 1-based CIL parameter. The tests come
# before the UTF-8 length loops and before the .try of msil_catch (5.20.8
# MX2), so no entry maps their exception, not even one that lists
# System.InvalidProgramException. A primitive value type (System.Int32
# here) is never an enum, so its test is only the throw, and the stub
# always throws. Plan 5.17.4's rule on loud
# failures: a declaration error that no tool can see fails loudly.
# Without the tests the struct ran by accident on the .NET Framework 4.8
# (the integer stood in for the TimeSpan) and threw InvalidProgramException
# without a message on .NET 8 and .NET 10, the wrong widths ran on every
# runtime, the catch stub mapping FileStream's FileNotFoundException to its
# code 2, and the long form of int32 named no member
# (MissingMethodException). At -O0 and -O2, for each program: clang -S, and
# clang -flto -c with an --lto-emit-asm link that passes no reference
# (%{msil_ref_flags} is empty whatever the leg), each text assembled by
# %ilasm -exe; each image runs on the configured runtime and on it again
# with DOTNET_TieredCompilation=0 (the optimizing JIT), is force-JITted
# (jitall compiles the stubs: their checks are ordinary code) and runs on
# each runtime of the leg's msil_also_run by %{msil_also_run_check}, and
# with msil_run_netfx on the .NET Framework 4.8. The images are not
# verified: the member still gets the integer where it takes E, which
# ILVerify and PEVerify report for the struct. The transcript is the status
# line alone: the programs print nothing before the call, and an unhandled
# exception loses the C library's buffered stdout. The STRUCT, WIDTH, CATCH
# and PRIMITIVE lines match the stub's own message in the runtime's report
# on stderr (the msil_also_run runs check the transcript only). No composite
# builds this test, so no equivalence oracle compares the text with an
# object link. Plan 5.17.13 (MC-1, M3/13-managed-calls).
# REDEFINE: %{msil_ref_flags} =
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# DEFINE: %{ep_prog} = struct
# DEFINE: %{ep_loud} = STRUCT
# DEFINE: %{ep_level} = O0
# DEFINE: %{ep_dir} = %t/%{ep_prog}-%{ep_level}
# DEFINE: %{ep_form} = text
# DEFINE: %{ep_image} = %{ep_dir}/%{ep_form}
# REDEFINE: %{msil_also_run_image} = %{ep_image}.exe
# DEFINE: %{ep_build} = \
# DEFINE:   mkdir -p %{ep_dir} \
# DEFINE:   && %clang_msil %{msil_cflags} -%{ep_level} -S %t/%{ep_prog}.c -o %{ep_dir}/text.il \
# DEFINE:   && %ilasm -exe -output=%{ep_dir}/text.exe %{ep_dir}/text.il \
# DEFINE:   && %clang_msil %{msil_cflags} -%{ep_level} -flto -c %t/%{ep_prog}.c -o %{ep_dir}/main.o \
# DEFINE:   && %clang_msil -%{ep_level} %{msil_ldflags} -Wl,--lto-emit-asm %{ep_dir}/main.o -o %{ep_dir}/lto.il \
# DEFINE:   && %ilasm -exe -output=%{ep_dir}/lto.exe %{ep_dir}/lto.il
# DEFINE: %{ep_run} = \
# DEFINE:   %msil_exec --stderr-out %{ep_image}.err --out %{ep_image}.out %{ep_image}.exe \
# DEFINE:   && FileCheck --input-file=%{ep_image}.out --match-full-lines %s \
# DEFINE:   && FileCheck --input-file=%{ep_image}.err --check-prefix=%{ep_loud} %s \
# DEFINE:   && %msil_exec --env DOTNET_TieredCompilation=0 --stderr-out %{ep_image}.tc0.err --out %{ep_image}.tc0.out %{ep_image}.exe \
# DEFINE:   && FileCheck --input-file=%{ep_image}.tc0.out --match-full-lines %s \
# DEFINE:   && FileCheck --input-file=%{ep_image}.tc0.err --check-prefix=%{ep_loud} %s \
# DEFINE:   %{msil_also_run_check}
# DEFINE: %{ep_netfx} = \
# DEFINE:   %msil_exec --netfx %{msil_netfx_skip} --stderr-out %{ep_image}.netfx.err --out %{ep_image}.netfx.out %{ep_image}.exe \
# DEFINE:   && FileCheck --input-file=%{ep_image}.netfx.out --match-full-lines %s \
# DEFINE:   && FileCheck --input-file=%{ep_image}.netfx.err --check-prefix=%{ep_loud} %s
